651
00:36:59,346 --> 00:37:03,060
So we will use
reinforcement learning.

652
00:37:03,060 --> 00:37:04,170
How does it work?

653
00:37:04,170 --> 00:37:06,660
This is the most generic form.

654
00:37:06,660 --> 00:37:10,680
The idea this is the most
generic definition of RL.

655
00:37:10,680 --> 00:37:14,270
The idea is for a
given policy, which

656
00:37:14,270 --> 00:37:18,450
is generate the next token,
we generate this next token,

657
00:37:18,450 --> 00:37:22,760
we interact with an
environment, we get some reward

658
00:37:22,760 --> 00:37:26,640
from the environment if that
generated token was good or bad,

659
00:37:26,640 --> 00:37:28,970
and then update the
state of the world.

660
00:37:28,970 --> 00:37:34,850
In RLHF, the state is getting
updated from the prompts

661
00:37:34,850 --> 00:37:39,680
that are getting
fed into the policy.

662
00:37:39,680 --> 00:37:46,340
The action is updating and
finding what responses are.

663
00:37:46,340 --> 00:37:48,500
And then the
environment is actually

664
00:37:48,500 --> 00:37:55,070
a reward model where it
tells us how good a model--

665
00:37:55,070 --> 00:37:57,860
tries to up a model
that preferences

666
00:37:57,860 --> 00:38:01,980
that this response is generally
preferred over the other one.

667
00:38:01,980 --> 00:38:05,720
So this is of how RLHF works.

668
00:38:05,720 --> 00:38:09,680
This reference data will fit
into a reward model, where

669
00:38:09,680 --> 00:38:12,650
reward model is actually
a neural network that

670
00:38:12,650 --> 00:38:16,880
is trained to tell us, for a
given prompt, which response

671
00:38:16,880 --> 00:38:18,260
is better?

672
00:38:18,260 --> 00:38:19,340
OK.

673
00:38:19,340 --> 00:38:24,900
How do we optimize this complex
situation through PPO training?

674
00:38:24,900 --> 00:38:26,910
Let's dig a little bit deeper.

675
00:38:26,910 --> 00:38:31,190
The idea is we want to
maximize the reward.

676
00:38:31,190 --> 00:38:36,770
We want to get the maximum
reward as possible such

677
00:38:36,770 --> 00:38:41,210
that we want to constrain
the model to stay as close as

678
00:38:41,210 --> 00:38:43,410
possible to the baseline model.

679
00:38:43,410 --> 00:38:49,100
We want the policy to don't go
that far from the originally

680
00:38:49,100 --> 00:38:50,455
trained model.

681
00:38:50,455 --> 00:38:53,630
So this is establishing
a very important balance

682
00:38:53,630 --> 00:38:57,680
between make sure you are
aligned with those preferences

683
00:38:57,680 --> 00:38:59,040
that are provided to you.

684
00:38:59,040 --> 00:39:03,380
However, don't go too far
from the original model

685
00:39:03,380 --> 00:39:06,590
that you have in mind.

686
00:39:06,590 --> 00:39:10,700
Now, in the last year or
so, many different variants

687
00:39:10,700 --> 00:39:16,220
are introduced on how to
